  "_about_embed_widths": "Embedding models known to be trained so the leading part of a vector is a usable vector of its own (Matryoshka / MRL), with their full width. Only these are cut to a narrower width (models.embed.dimensions; the default for them is 1024, measured 2026-10-13 in docs/rag/embedding-width-2026-10.md). A model not listed keeps its full width: cutting a model that was not trained for it ruins its search quality. Keys are matched by ReferenceName (lower case, after the last '/', without ':variant'). Sources: the Qwen3-Embedding model card (MRL, 32 up to the full width), OpenAI's embeddings guide (text-embedding-3 'dimensions'), Google's Gemini embeddings guide (gemini-embedding-001 output_dimensionality).",
  "embed_widths": {
